 ### [Octree Neighbor Finding](1821-octree-neighbor-finding.md)
-Octree Neighbor Finding determines the adjacent leaf nodes in six cardinal directions (±X, ±Y, ±Z) for a given node in a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO). It solves the problem of traversing between non-contiguous or differently-sized nodes during ray casting or pathfinding by locating the nearest shared ancestor and performing point location to retrieve the neighbor. It differs from sibling methods like [Morton Key Vertex Neighbor Iteration](3318-morton-key-vertex-neighbor-iteration.md) by relying on explicit parent-pointer traversal (via a trace array) and coordinate bit-masking rather than Morton key arithmetic.
