-### [Sparse Voxel Octree Ray Traversal](2451-sparse-voxel-octree-ray-traversal.md)
-Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) Ray Traversal is a hierarchical ray-casting algorithm that traverses a 3D sparse voxel octree to find the first occupied leaf node (voxel) intersected by a ray. It solves the problem of efficiently rendering large, sparse 3D volumes by skipping empty space and adapting resolution based on viewer distance (implicit Level-of-Detail). It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Sparse Voxel Octree Ray Tracing](2989-sparse-voxel-octree-ray-tracing.md) by using a fixed-point-like scale representation and bit-manipulation for coordinate alignment, rather than explicit stack-based scale management, and differs from [Sparse Voxel Octree Ray Traversal (State Machine)](3299-sparse-voxel-octree-ray-traversal-state-machine.md) by using a deterministic iterative approach with explicit goto-based control flow or standard loop structures rather than a finite state machine.
 
